1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Football is social, but most live sports products are passive.
VIRA turns real match events into synchronized multiplayer decisions for friends.

2
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:33,000
One fan makes a pre-match pick and creates a visual invite directly from the product.

3
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:45,000
A friend joins instantly as a guest — no wallet, social account, payment or installation.

4
00:00:45,000 --> 00:01:09,000
Both participants arrive in the same Match Room and share one authoritative match state.

5
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:17,000
Optional Web Push can bring fans back when a round opens.

6
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:35,000
Every participant receives the same structured question and the same server-synchronized countdown.

7
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:53,000
Answers remain private until lock. The server accepts one eligible response per participant.

8
00:01:53,000 --> 00:02:07,000
The deadline belongs to the authoritative runtime. Late or duplicate submissions cannot rewrite the state.

9
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:29,000
Demo input: captured TxLINE test fixture.
The same normalization pipeline resolves the structured rule for everyone.

10
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:35,000
Points and ranking converge from the same resolved room state.

11
00:02:35,000 --> 00:03:02,000
TxLINE fixtures, scores, updates and market data flow through normalization, runtime and SSE to fans.

12
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:14,000
Official Review reproduces the ledger, projection, result and ranking without misrepresenting input origin.

13
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:30,000
Fans participate for free. Partners fund branded match experiences and measurable engagement.

14
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:40,000
VIRA — a verifiable multiplayer participation layer for live football, powered by TxLINE.
